  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "If the $15$th term of an arithmetic series is $-53$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $-777,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=-777$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -777 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ -1\\,554= & 21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $15$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{15} & ={a}_{1}+(15-1)d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-53={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -74=2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}106 & =-2{a}_{1}-28d \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ 32 & =-8d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-53 & ={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14(-4) \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}-56 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
